1
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone who's broke, come to me!

2
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,980
I've got nothing either, so don't worry!

3
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:36,060
Look, blue skies and white clouds!

4
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:36,440
Me

5
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:42,960
We'll manage somehow, right?

6
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to me!

7
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,480
I've got nothing either, so don't worry!

8
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:43,780
Blast those crooked salesmen away!

9
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,600
What is it, Terai?

10
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,260
What on earth is going on here?

11
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:03,980
Did you get that catalog too?

12
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,640
Whatever the case, that's just too cruel.

13
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,580
Deceiving me, a fellow officer like this!

14
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,700
What's wrong, Terai-san?

15
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,500
Did Ryo-chan do something to you?

16
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:14,060
Listen, Reiko-san, Nakagawa-kun!

17
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:17,600
Three days ago, Ryo-san told me
about a brand-new 200,000-yen computer

18
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:20,860
and offered to let me have it for
half price if I paid cash right away.

19
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:22,040
He invited me to buy it.

20
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:25,660
If the latest model is half price,
isn't that a good deal?

21
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:30,060
But when I looked at this mail-order catalog
they were handing out at the station today,

22
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:33,920
Look, it was really 70,000 yen.

23
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:37,660
So you skimmed 30,000 yen off it too,
Ryo-chan?

24
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:40,580
Hey, don't say such nasty things.

25
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:42,180
Look at this carefully.

26
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:47,760
It's only cheap because I gathered five or more customers,
isn't it?

27
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:51,900
Someone who made that effort
getting 30,000 yen isn't unreasonable.

28
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:52,760
I see.

29
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:54,200
Wait a moment.

30
00:02:54,200 --> 00:03:00,000
At 30,000 yen per person, five people means
150,000 yen goes into your pocket, senior.

31
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:05,800
So just gathering buyers and making
150,000 yen is basically fraud.

32
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:09,460
Don't be stupid.
Think it over carefully, Terai.

33
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:12,700
The company profits too,
since five of its surplus computers sold.

34
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:16,340
You benefit as well, getting a
200,000 yen computer for half price.

35
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:16,600
Mm.

36
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:19,520
And I profit 30,000 yen per unit.

37
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:19,920
Mm.

38
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:23,220
Nobody's losing out
while everybody's gaining.

39
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:23,920
Mm-hmm.

40
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:27,620
Then it works out nicely for everyone,
doesn't it?

41
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:29,500
Now that you mention it,

42
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:32,060
Terai, don't let yourself be fooled!

43
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:34,320
It's unnecessary for
Ryo-chan to profit from it!

44
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:35,600
That's right.

45
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:41,380
If you find four more people who want a computer,
Terai, you can buy one for 70,000 yen.

46
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:42,320
I see.

47
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:44,620
Don't go filling his
head with useless ideas!

48
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:49,600
Anyway, the computer money was already transferred yesterday,
so it's too late now.

49
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:50,200
No way...

50
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:53,000
What's all the commotion about?

51
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:53,620
Chief.

52
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:54,900
Good morning.

53
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:56,500
Morning.

54
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:59,480
Listen to me, Ryo-san!

55
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,920
Sorry, I've got to go. I'm on patrol.

56
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,200
Wait, Ryo-chan.

57
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:06,060
Chief, that...

58
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:09,300
Actually,
there's something I need you to do.

59
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:12,560
Hey, Terai-kun, come in.

60
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:13,560
Yes.

61
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:18,080
Nice to meet you.

62
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:22,160
Chief, what's this limp-wristed guy?

63
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:25,420
Sorry. Please forgive me.

64
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,180
What's with this guy?

65
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:31,000
This is Officer Terai,
who's just been assigned to our station.

66
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,640
Nice to meet you, I'm Reiko Akimoto.
Pleased to meet you.

67
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:36,600
The pleasure is mine.

68
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:40,000
You're a beautiful woman.

69
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,060
I'm Keiichi Nakagawa.

70
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,780
You're so cool.

71
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:46,320
This police box is like a modeling agency.

72
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:48,500
I'm Yoichi Terai.

73
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:49,980
Not really, is it?

74
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:54,160
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

75
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:58,560
As you can see, Terai is a bit timid.

76
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:02,660
The chief asked me to
help him get over that.

77
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:04,880
W-wait,
you mean I'm the one who has to do that?

78
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:05,860
You catch on quick.

79
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,205
Anyway,

80
00:05:07,255 --> 00:05:10,300
toughen him up for me.

81
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:11,520
Terai.

82
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:12,300
Y-yes?

83
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,560
Senior Officer Ryotsu
here will be training you.

84
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:18,180
Nice to meet you, Senior Officer Ryotsu.

85
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:23,060
Hey! Walk faster, Terai.

86
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:25,360
Yes! Senpai is just fast.

87
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:28,820
My pace is the standard
speed for a Japanese person.

88
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,680
Pleased to meet you.

89
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:31,340
No thanks!

90
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:32,500
What is it?

91
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,920
No thanks!

92
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:34,500
Yikes!

93
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:35,560
No thanks!

94
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,560
Whoa! Get out of the way!

95
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:39,220
Whoa!

96
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:41,320
Yes.

97
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:41,880
Thanks.

98
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:42,760
Here you go.

99
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:43,340
Sorry.

100
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:44,180
Nice to meet you.

101
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:44,740
Thank you.

102
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:48,600
Listen up. Police officers must
always hold their heads high.

103
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:53,180
You shouldn't be saying nonsense like
"a police force loved by the citizens."

104
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:53,920
Senpai.

105
00:05:57,820 --> 00:05:59,200
What are you doing?

106
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:02,100
I can't see! Please help me!

107
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:03,960
Got it!

108
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:06,100
Thank you, that saved me.

109
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:08,100
Why don't you refuse them?

110
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:09,900
I was going to refuse, but...

111
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:12,580
I felt bad, like I had to take them.

112
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:13,340
You idiot!

113
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:15,900
They're part-timers who only
get paid if they hand these out!

114
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:18,160
And there are idiots who go
along with them for a while.

115
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:19,740
Sorry.

116
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,700
Terai, don't leave my side!

117
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:22,380
Yes.

118
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:29,440
Hey, hey, young man!

119
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:31,680
Me?

120
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,080
This latest model

121
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:35,260
is a fully automatic sewing
machine with a built-in computer.

122
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:39,420
Normally, this would cost 150,000 yen,
but just this once,

123
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:42,260
it's only 80,000 yen!

124
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,380
That's cheap!

125
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:47,540
Right? Look, just like this.

126
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,480
Just place the fabric
and it can sew anything.

127
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:52,160
That looks handy.

128
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:55,240
Right? How about one?

129
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:58,200
But I never use a sewing machine, you know.

130
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:01,720
Well, you've got me there, customer.
You're a skilled negotiator.

131
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:05,720
I'll knock off another 10,000 yen,
so let's settle on 70,000 yen.

132
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:09,700
Honestly, I can't beat you, customer.

133
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:13,300
In that case, I'll throw in
this sewing set as a free bonus.

134
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:15,060
Here, 70,000 yen.

135
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:23,080
70,000 Well,
I happen to have exactly 70,000 yen.

136
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:23,620
Thank you for your business.

137
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:28,380
That idiot has gone missing again!

138
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:29,320
Senpai.

139
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:33,000
Senpai.

140
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,240
What's that supposed to mean?

141
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:38,180
It's a sewing machine.

142
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:40,980
You don't go shopping while on patrol!

143
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:42,000
No, it's not like that.

144
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,260
I didn't realize it until I'd
already been made to buy it.

145
00:07:44,260 --> 00:07:44,880
What?

146
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:48,220
I've never even used
a sewing machine before.

147
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:49,380
I see.

148
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:51,340
That personality of yours is the problem.

149
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,080
Alright.

150
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:53,480
Follow me.

151
00:07:54,060 --> 00:07:54,500
Yes.

152
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,320
Come on, come on!

153
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,740
Hey there, ladies!

154
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:00,680
Together, yeah!

155
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,560
W-what is it?

156
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:04,840
Here, I'm returning this.

157
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:07,660
This guy bought it by mistake.

158
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:09,160
I'm cancelling it.

159
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,440
But that's a problem, you know.

160
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:13,960
Since it's already been sold once,

161
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:16,040
Shall I say it again?

162
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,480
It's cancelled.

163
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,340
Yes, right away.

164
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:20,960
Thank you very much.

165
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:24,700
Thanks to you, I got my 70,000 yen back.

166
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:26,780
You should've just refused it yourself.

167
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:29,560
But I felt bad about turning him down.

168
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:34,380
Just say
"No," while staring the other person straight in the eye.

169
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:35,560
Got it?

170
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:42,780
In Tokyo, where people will snatch the eyes out of a living horse,
you can't survive unless you clearly assert yourself.

171
00:08:42,780 --> 00:08:44,100
Yes, I understand.

172
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:45,700
Right, let's go.

173
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:46,500
Yes.

174
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:49,000
Gotchon-gotchon-go

175
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,560
Gotchon-go

176
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:50,800
Gotchon-go

177
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,300
Gotchon-go

178
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:53,180
Ow ow!

179
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:54,360
Welcome!

180
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,680
Well...

181
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,700
We have an easy-to-read menu right here.

182
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:01,820
Damn, it looks like he's
going to get away again.

183
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:05,660
Right, just like Senpai told me,
look them in the eye.

184
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:10,660
How about our newly released 10-burger set?

185
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:13,980
Yes, then, that one.

186
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:16,480
Ate it, ate it, ate it!

187
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:20,040
Would you like freshly
fried potatoes with that?

188
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:22,660
Please.

189
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,800
Honestly, that guy's gone off somewhere again,
where'd he go?

190
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:31,780
There you are, Terai.
Did they make you buy stuff again?

191
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:34,820
I can't eat ten hamburgers.

192
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:37,080
Well, there's no help for it.
I'll give you a hand.

193
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:37,780
Sorry.

194
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:41,020
Yeah, it's just about lunchtime anyway.

195
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,460
Hey, what about the drinks?

196
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,000
Hey,

197
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:47,600
Look, you don't have to eat it all. They'll
just have you buying useless stuff again.

198
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:51,560
Then why don't you come to my room?
I have juice, at least.

199
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:54,900
You live in an apartment like this?

200
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:59,320
It's barely three minutes from the station,
so the rent must be pretty high, right?

201
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,060
It's 200,000 yen.

202
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:02,700
200,000 yen!?

203
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:05,720
The real estate agent pushed it on me,
and I couldn't say no.

204
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:09,760
Hey, hey, hey,
who stacks up newspapers like this?

205
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:12,980
These are all today's
commissioner's papers, though.

206
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:15,920
When they give me detergent and things,
I can't say no.

207
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,260
Here you go.

208
00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:21,240
W-what is this room?

209
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:24,480
Stuff I was pressured into buying from
mail order and catch sales has piled up,

210
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:26,020
and it's ended up like this.

211
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:27,260
What?

212
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,840
Hey, you don't need this many
fire extinguishers, do you?

213
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,720
The lady who came to sell them to me

214
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,680
was such an unfortunate person

215
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,140
that she'd actually lost her husband

216
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:40,880
and my parents are also in the
hospital from a car accident.

217
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,900
If you don't buy these...

218
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:44,720
I'll have no choice but to hang myself.

219
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:45,660
Understood.

220
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:47,100
Then, one, please.

221
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:48,540
Just one?

222
00:10:50,260 --> 00:10:51,760
If it's just one...

223
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:54,300
I guess I'll hang myself after all...

224
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:57,120
Fine, I'll buy it. I'll buy all of them!

225
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:57,980
Thank you very much.

226
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,720
That's obviously a lie!

227
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,640
What is all this?!

228
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:08,720
Sorry.

229
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:12,440
English conversation training videos?

230
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:15,740
Are you planning to become an
English teacher or something?!

231
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:18,440
Sorry. It's not just English.

232
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:22,560
I was also made to buy tapes of
every foreign language in the world.

233
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:26,440
Right, French, Norwegian, Vietnamese...

234
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:31,540
Correct Edo dialect? What were you thinking?

235
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,140
I just end up buying them somehow.

236
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:36,760
And this here is a gravestone

237
00:11:36,760 --> 00:11:37,420
Yes.

238
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:40,040
Why is something like this in your room?

239
00:11:40,460 --> 00:11:44,920
I passed a stone monument shop, and they
said it was a once-every-four-years mega sale.

240
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,940
It's not like the Olympics, you know.

241
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:48,060
Sorry.

242
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:51,240
Even if you bought a gravestone,
do you even have a cemetery plot?

243
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:54,420
They even made me buy a
grave on a ten-year loan.

244
00:11:56,300 --> 00:11:56,860
Mmmmph!

245
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:57,820
Mmph!

246
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:58,980
S-senpai!

247
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:00,800
Whoa!

248
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:03,780
Then what on earth is this portable toilet?

249
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:07,040
A room like this should have a toilet and a bath,
shouldn't it?

250
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:08,120
Well, that's the thing...

251
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:10,860
This is the toilet?

252
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,880
There's a bath in the back too, but...

253
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:16,860
With encyclopedias, art collections,
literature collections,

254
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:18,800
they've filled it all up, just like this.

255
00:12:19,220 --> 00:12:20,900
You could open a library with this!

256
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:27,180
Ugh, forget it.
I've lost even the will to get angry.

257
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,680
Wherever I look, there's junk everywhere.

258
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:36,760
Geez, sit down, I can't sit down, a

259
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:47,020
Most of the stuff in this room is mail-order, isn't it?
Yes, you can't see it because of the piano, but there's also a waterbed and a tropical fish set in the back.

260
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:50,220
Nobody's forced me to buy
them from salesmen, though.

261
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:52,060
Why do you go and buy so much?

262
00:12:52,060 --> 00:12:54,660
Mail-order direct mail comes every day,

263
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:56,920
I'm sure it's around here somewhere.

264
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:59,720
Here it is.
They come in like this, you know.

265
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:00,860
In a single day?

266
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:01,300
Yeah.

267
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:05,320
Every one of them has
a reply postcard inside,

268
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:08,740
and if you send this one back,
the goods are guaranteed to arrive.

269
00:13:08,740 --> 00:13:11,280
Of course they do, it's an order postcard!

270
00:13:12,180 --> 00:13:15,020
But it says to send it back within
a certain number of days, too.

271
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:17,560
feeling good about myself,

272
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,580
you don't have to take it out.

273
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:22,980
That's exactly why your room
ends up stuffed full of junk.

274
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:23,800
Sorry.

275
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:26,600
My throat is so dry, I'm parched.

276
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:29,000
Right, you said you had juice, didn't you?

277
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:30,580
This way, please.

278
00:13:31,860 --> 00:13:34,780
I think it was this fridge, right?

279
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:36,140
Found it.

280
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:37,260
Here you go.

281
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:43,660
By the way, that hurts.

282
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:44,240
Yes.

283
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:44,420
Yes.

284
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:46,960
Why do you have three refrigerators?

285
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:50,800
The other day, I was walking through the
electronics store and got talked into buying them.

286
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:52,460
How do you even have the money?

287
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:54,540
Almost all of them are on loans.

288
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:57,863
Loans or not,
if you keep buying this much stuff,

289
00:13:57,913 --> 00:13:59,600
the monthly payments must
be a nightmare, right?

290
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:01,520
Well, that's the thing...

291
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,460
Please take a look at this.

292
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:05,560
Menko cards? That brings back memories.

293
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:08,320
No, these are credit cards.

294
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:11,280
W-what, you have this many?!

295
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:15,960
They just piled up before I knew it, and
even paying the annual fees is a struggle.

296
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,400
Roughly estimating,
there must be at least a thousand of them.

297
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:21,280
How am I supposed to
make a living from now on?

298
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:26,940
Anyway, which mail-order items
arrived within the last 8 days?

299
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:33,520
The world art collection, the athletic equipment,
and the CD/MD component system...

300
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:36,180
List them all.
You can return every one of them.

301
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:39,040
There's a system called "cooling-off,"

302
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:43,860
so most things can be cancelled
if you haven't used them yet.

303
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:46,340
R-really? You can do that too?

304
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:48,820
You didn't even read the contracts, did you?

305
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:51,860
It's always written in every contract,

306
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:53,220
down in the corner.

307
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:54,480
I didn't know that.

308
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:58,180
I'll cancel every one of those
credit card companies for you.

309
00:14:58,980 --> 00:14:59,420
Thank you so much.

310
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,200
Good work.

311
00:15:07,140 --> 00:15:08,280
Right then.

312
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:09,620
Thank you very much.

313
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,640
It's cleaned up a bit,
but there's still a lot left.

314
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:17,060
We'll just have to force
them to take it back.

315
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:23,420
You want to return them?

316
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:25,380
All of this?

317
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:27,740
It's all unused.

318
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:28,560
But -

319
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:30,360
Go get the store manager.

320
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:30,960
Yes.

321
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:33,640
Leave it to me.

322
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:36,580
I'm incredibly good at
this kind of negotiation.

323
00:15:37,980 --> 00:15:38,420
Amazing.

324
00:15:39,260 --> 00:15:42,620
I can't believe you actually made
them take back all those items.

325
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:48,280
But the real hassle is the stuff you
were pushed into buying around this town.

326
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,620
Sorry.

327
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:53,200
Let's go to the place where you're
always getting caught by catch-sales.

328
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:53,860
Yes.

329
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,680
They're often here on Sundays.

330
00:15:57,480 --> 00:15:59,900
This place is the Ginza of catch-sales.

331
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:04,340
Well, the same guys should be here for sure.

332
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:05,880
You too, you dummy.

333
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:09,420
He's gone! Damn, did he already get caught?

334
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:11,360
Where? Hey, there he is!

335
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:14,420
If you become a member, travel, hotels,

336
00:16:14,470 --> 00:16:17,040
movies, everything is at a special rate.

337
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,340
Wow, that's amazing.

338
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:21,480
Most young people have already joined,
you know.

339
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:24,740
Really? Then I'll join.

340
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,980
Senpai.

341
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:29,220
Look, there he is!
Tell him you don't need it!

342
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:33,540
But there's no entrance fee or membership dues,
you can join for free.

343
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:35,880
That's right.

344
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:40,320
Hey, you're not going to charge us a membership maintenance fee or something,
are you?

345
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:45,160
No, it's just a tiny amount.
It's only about 20,000 yen a month.

346
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:47,540
That's 240,000 yen a year!

347
00:16:48,780 --> 00:16:51,740
You didn't say a word about that!

348
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,800
Look, there's no such thing as a free lunch...
and nothing costs more than something free.

349
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,500
So then, I'm just going to...

350
00:16:57,500 --> 00:17:01,620
Hold on! Don't you guys also
sell language learning materials?

351
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:06,820
Yes. Would you like to make use of
our authentic Edo dialect course?

352
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,080
Wait right there!

353
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:14,100
I was made to buy it at your place,
and I'm cancelling it!

354
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:16,780
Ah, that's impossible.

355
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:19,620
Look, Article 125 of the application form...

356
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:23,220
If you read it carefully,
there are exceptions too.

357
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:25,120
Let's cancel, cancel.

358
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:28,440
One educational video, cancelled, done.

359
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:29,780
Right, next.

360
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:31,320
Again.

361
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:34,640
Hey, what exactly do you sell at your place?

362
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:36,260
Fashion rings.

363
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:38,240
They're not on the returns list.

364
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,540
Let's go.

365
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:43,320
Right now, luxury gemstones are super cheap!

366
00:17:43,320 --> 00:17:43,900
No thanks.

367
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,580
He ran off with just one word.

368
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:50,880
That's why I'm telling you, just say
"No thanks."

369
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:53,380
Excuse me,
do you have a moment for a survey?

370
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:55,860
I'm busy, so no. Try someone else.

371
00:17:55,860 --> 00:17:57,060
Sorry to bother you.

372
00:17:58,020 --> 00:18:02,060
Come on, a quick survey won't hurt!
And you were such a beauty, too.

373
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:05,380
That's why you're hopeless.
Look, watch this.

374
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:11,520
See? An innocent-looking young guy
like you has already been caught.

375
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,320
You're right.

376
00:18:14,980 --> 00:18:16,960
They're going into a café.

377
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:19,540
Keep watching from a distance.
It starts now.

378
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:23,020
At first they act like they're on a date,

379
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:24,720
He's on the phone.

380
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:26,820
Someone's coming.

381
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:29,200
They swapped for a man.

382
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:32,500
Try being worked on by
two men for two hours.

383
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:34,300
Most people fall for it.

384
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:36,780
That woman is, so to speak, the bait.

385
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:39,240
I went through the same thing.

386
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:42,320
In my case,
I signed up in just three minutes.

387
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,620
Don't get cocky, you idiot!

388
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:44,820
Sorry.

389
00:18:44,820 --> 00:18:50,800
There's also the one where a woman calls
saying you've won a prize and invites you out.

390
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:52,420
That one too, several times.

391
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:54,140
Honestly.

392
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:55,480
Excuse me.

393
00:18:56,540 --> 00:19:04,660
Other things they made you buy here were a 100-volume art encyclopedia set,
a bodybuilding set, and a grand piano, right?

394
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:05,120
Alright.

395
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:07,360
What are you doing?

396
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:11,900
I'd love a complete art collection.

397
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:14,640
And I want a bodybuilding set too.

398
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:17,160
I'd also like to travel overseas cheaply.

399
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:19,820
I can't decide how to spend my money.

400
00:19:21,060 --> 00:19:21,860
Senpai.

401
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:23,360
Hey, hey.

402
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:25,440
We have art collections.

403
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:30,100
For a bodybuilding set, you should definitely come to us,
and we do overseas trips too.

404
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:31,600
Now's your chance.

405
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:35,660
Which of these places handles grand pianos?

406
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:45,640
Only ours. If you can't repay the loan, you can return the piano.
It says here they may even buy it back as a used item.

407
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:48,160
Well, that just means it's
a possibility in some cases.

408
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:59,360
Well, that's unthinkable, yes.

409
00:19:59,360 --> 00:19:59,620
Yes.

410
00:20:01,560 --> 00:20:02,240
Don't run away!

411
00:20:02,780 --> 00:20:05,480
The Kenpei are much scarier.

412
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:08,800
Wow, so you got rid of everything?

413
00:20:09,230 --> 00:20:12,780
The items no one would take,
I sold to a secondhand shop.

414
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:17,280
Because of that,
Terai's room is totally empty now.

415
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:22,500
But Terai, you also have a problem,
buying anything so easily.

416
00:20:23,010 --> 00:20:24,860
That's the root of it.

417
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:28,920
With Terai's personality,
it probably won't ever be cured, will it?

418
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:34,900
Don't worry, with my idea,
nobody can force you to buy anything.

419
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,820
How did you do it?

420
00:20:36,820 --> 00:20:38,940
Senpai, please help me.

421
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:43,920
There are two Ryo-chans!

422
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,720
I'm Terai.

423
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:46,860
Terai-san.

424
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:53,120
I had a costume company I know
make a mask that looks just like me.

425
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:58,420
So with your face,
the catch-sales people won't come near

426
00:20:58,420 --> 00:20:59,720
Exactly.

427
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:02,320
But it hurts, you know.
What on earth happened?

428
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:05,900
True, the catch-sales people
have stopped coming over, but

429
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:08,560
when I tried to do some
shopping around here,

430
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:12,340
"Until you pay your tab, Ryo-san,
I won't sell you a thing!"

431
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:16,020
"Not until you bring the
ramen money you've piled up!"

432
00:21:16,020 --> 00:21:18,000
"Don't you dare dirty our noren!"

433
00:21:19,520 --> 00:21:21,880
"Don't show me that face until you pay up!"

434
00:21:22,020 --> 00:21:22,760
"Get out! Get out!"

435
00:21:24,860 --> 00:21:27,220
I went through absolute hell.

436
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:30,640
You've really stiffed a lot of
people on their debts, senpai.

437
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:33,620
I'm done with wearing this face.

438
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:34,680
Ryo-san

439
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:37,040
It's bad, Ryo-san!

440
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:38,420
What is it, Terai?

441
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:39,740
Look at this.

442
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:44,020
A shady mail-order company
has gone under on purpose.

443
00:21:44,020 --> 00:21:49,000
This company's name is the same as
the one in that catalog the other day.

444
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:49,460
What?

445
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:49,600
What?

446
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:57,120
The number you have dialed
is no longer in service.

447
00:21:57,120 --> 00:22:01,780
I've been scammed!
I transferred 350,000 yen!

448
00:22:02,100 --> 00:22:07,560
Ryo-san! If the computer isn't coming,
then give me back my 100,000 yen.

449
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:09,267
O-okay, Terai.

450
00:22:09,317 --> 00:22:12,480
But I've already spent the money I made,

451
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:13,760
Right.

452
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:16,300
Right.

453
00:22:16,300 --> 00:22:18,080
Yes.

454
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:20,840
Why don't you buy these cards?

455
00:22:21,620 --> 00:22:24,160
All of these cards are premium cards.

456
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:27,260
Among them are ones that go
for as much as 50,000 yen each,

457
00:22:27,260 --> 00:22:30,220
and there are even special cards that
collectors would cry tears of joy over.

458
00:22:30,580 --> 00:22:32,580
Altogether, they're worth a million yen!

459
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:36,080
Today, as a special deal, I'll knock
it down to 500,000 yen, so please,

460
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:37,120
buy them.

461
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:40,080
But I'm not interested in card games.

462
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:41,960
Just 300,000 yen will do.

463
00:22:43,760 --> 00:22:46,340
No, Terai. You have to refuse here.

464
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:50,240
Shut up! Terai, please,
think of it as helping someone.

465
00:22:51,560 --> 00:22:53,280
Terai, you have to refuse.

466
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:55,220
T-Terai.

467
00:22:57,360 --> 00:22:59,960
Look him in the eye and say,
"I don't need it!"

468
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:02,320
Hey, Terai, say, "I don't need it!"

469
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:04,760
So just say, "I don't need it!"

470
00:23:05,320 --> 00:23:07,143
I-I...

471
00:23:07,193 --> 00:23:09,380
I don't need it!

472
00:23:13,240 --> 00:23:14,860
I actually said no for once!

473
00:23:15,520 --> 00:23:17,100
Good job, Terai-san.

474
00:23:17,100 --> 00:23:18,840
See, you can do it when you try.

475
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:20,420
Yes, thank you very much.

476
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:22,200
Terai.

477
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:24,540
Then how about this helicopter?

478
00:23:24,540 --> 00:23:26,900
It's normally 500,000,
but you can have it for 100,000.

479
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:27,700
No thanks.

480
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:30,060
Terai.

481
00:23:30,060 --> 00:23:32,040
No, no, no, no!

482
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:36,560
You can refuse completely now!

483
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:41,880
Terai-san,
you've finally overcome your weakness.

484
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:44,700
Why can you only refuse when it's me?

485
00:23:44,700 --> 00:23:48,500
What are you talking about?
Ryo-chan is the one who trained me.

486
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:49,220
No way.

487
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:51,640
Ryo-san.

488
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:52,060
Gulp.

489
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:55,120
Give me back my 100,000 yen, okay?

490
00:23:56,680 --> 00:23:58,420
Terai, wait!

491
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:02,980
Say yes again, once more, just say yes!

492
00:24:15,140 --> 00:24:20,340
Like someone was calling out,
the day after the rain

493
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:27,200
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand

494
00:24:28,280 --> 00:24:34,560
That strange feeling I had back then

495
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:39,600
On the tiles of the arcade street

496
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:45,400
I tried walking only on the black ones

497
00:24:47,940 --> 00:24:51,560
Everyone was a child once

498
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:53,640
but everyone has forgotten

499
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:57,680
Not the politicians with
their self-important faces

500
00:24:57,680 --> 00:25:00,980
or the aunties with blue eyeshadow

501
00:25:00,980 --> 00:25:03,980
Why don't you turn

502
00:25:04,940 --> 00:25:06,580
at that corner

503
00:25:07,740 --> 00:25:11,780
I get to meet everyone, everyone!

504
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:12,980
Don't go!

505
00:25:12,980 --> 00:25:16,560
Over there is Kameari.

506
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:19,840
Kameari, the marked territory.

507
00:25:20,440 --> 00:25:24,920
Everyone, come on over to our town!

508
00:25:25,980 --> 00:25:26,540
Thank you.

509
00:25:29,860 --> 00:25:30,980
We did it!

510
00:25:30,980 --> 00:25:36,160
Look closely, the all-you-can-eat buffet
for just 500 yen is women-only, isn't it!

511
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:39,100
Damn, if only I'd been born a woman too!

512
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:42,500
If it's come to this,
I'll fight for true gender equality!

513
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:47,440
Next time, I'm an actress!
Ryoko Kameari, nice to meet you.

514
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:50,920
Over there is Kameari.

515
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:54,620
Well, surely Kameari.

516
00:25:55,400 --> 00:25:59,280
Everyone, come on over to our town!

517
00:26:00,340 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you.

